---
import AppLayout from '../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/app.css';
import '../styles/page.css';

const updated = 'August 2026';
const supportEmail = 'yash@typethink.ai';
---

<AppLayout
	title="Privacy Policy — doodleai.art"
	description="What doodleai.art stores (almost nothing — it's local to your browser), what goes to PicX and OpenRouter, and how to clear your data."
>
	<Navbar />

	<main class="page">
		<div class="page-hero">
			<div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
			<h1>Privacy <span class="grad">Policy</span></h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Short version: no accounts, nothing sold, and almost nothing stored on our servers at all —
				your chats, doodles, and saved photos live in your browser.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="prose">
			<p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {updated}</p>

			<h2>The short version</h2>
			<div class="facts">
				<div class="fact"><div class="k">Accounts</div><div class="v">None — no signup or login</div></div>
				<div class="fact"><div class="k">Data stored on our servers</div><div class="v">None</div></div>
				<div class="fact"><div class="k">Cookies</div><div class="v">Analytics only</div></div>
				<div class="fact"><div class="k">Ad pixels</div><div class="v">None</div></div>
				<div class="fact"><div class="k">Selling data</div><div class="v">Never</div></div>
			</div>

			<h2>What's stored, and where</h2>
			<p>
				doodleai.art is bring-your-own-key and stores its working data in your browser, not on
				our servers:
			</p>
			<ul class="steps">
				<li><b>In your browser's local storage only:</b> your PicX API key, your chat threads, your saved moodboard doodles, your saved "characters" (reference photos you've named for reuse), and small preferences like your theme and default style. This never leaves your device except as described below, and clearing your browser data removes all of it.</li>
				<li><b>Sent to PicX, under your own key:</b> any photo you attach in a chat. PicX hosts and processes it to generate or edit an image; the resulting image is served from PicX's own storage. PicX's handling of that data is governed by their own privacy policy, not ours.</li>
				<li><b>Sent to OpenRouter, for a single reply:</b> the text of your chat message (and any photo/reference URLs mentioned in it), so the doodle agent can decide what to draw. Our server does not keep a copy — conversation history is stored client-side, as above, and re-sent fresh with each message.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				We do not collect email addresses, names, or anything behind a login, because there is no
				login.
			</p>

			<h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
			<p>
				We use <a href="https://datafa.st" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DataFast</a>
				to understand how people find and use the site — which pages get visited and which sources
				send traffic. It records things like the page viewed, the referring source, and general
				device, browser, and country-level information.
			</p>
			<p>
				DataFast <strong>sets cookies</strong> to recognise a returning visitor so those numbers
				aren't wildly inflated. That is the only cookie-based tracking on the site. We do not run
				advertising pixels, we are not part of an ad network, and we never sell or share this data.
				You can block or clear these cookies in your browser settings at any time; the site works
				fine without them. See
				<a href="https://datafa.st/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DataFast's privacy policy</a>
				for how they handle it as our processor.
			</p>

			<h2>Who processes it</h2>
			<ul class="steps">
				<li><b>Cloudflare</b> — hosting for the site and its API routes.</li>
				<li><b>PicX</b> — image generation, editing, and hosting, under your own API key.</li>
				<li><b>OpenRouter</b> — the language model behind the chat agent.</li>
				<li><b>DataFast</b> — website analytics.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Local storage on your device</h2>
			<p>
				Beyond the analytics cookies above, everything doodleai.art remembers is kept in your
				browser's local storage: your PicX API key, chat threads, moodboard, saved characters, and a
				few interface preferences (theme, default style, sidebar state). None of it is an account
				identifier tied to you by us, none of it leaves your device except the specific requests
				described above, and clearing your browser data removes all of it instantly.
			</p>

			<h2>Server logs</h2>
			<p>
				Our host processes standard request data such as IP address and user agent to serve traffic
				and block abuse. We do not build profiles from it or use it for advertising.
			</p>

			<h2>Clearing your data</h2>
			<div class="callout">
				<p>
					Since nothing is stored on our servers, there's nothing for us to delete on your behalf.
					Delete individual items directly in the app (Moodboards and Characters both have a remove
					button), or clear your browser's site data for doodleai.art to remove everything at
					once. To remove a photo already sent to PicX, manage it through your own PicX account.
				</p>
			</div>

			<h2>Children</h2>
			<p>
				This site is not directed at children. If you believe a minor has used it in a way that
				concerns you, email us and we'll look into it.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>
				If this policy changes, the date at the top will change with it.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Privacy questions:
				<a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="page-cta">
			<a href="/">Back to the app</a>
		</div>
	</main>

	<Footer />

	<script>
		import { initThemeToggle } from '../lib/theme';
		const themeToggle = document.getElementById('themeToggle');
		if (themeToggle) initThemeToggle(themeToggle);
	</script>
</AppLayout>
